<title>NETHERLANDS: ING TO CONTINUE COMMODITY, METALS CLEARING.</title>
<headline>ING TO CONTINUE COMMODITY, METALS CLEARING.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Groep NV said on Tuesday its ING Futures and Options unit was withdrawing from sales of commodity derivatives brokerage services but it would continue providing clearing services for commodities and metals.</p>
<p>ING spokesman Wieger Sietsma earlier told Reuters the unit was withdrawing from sales of brokerage and clearing services for commodity derivatives, with the loss of 40 jobs in Chicago and four in London, in a reorganisation of the unit.</p>
<p>But he later corrected this, saying: &quot;We will continue to provide clearing services in commodities and metals.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
